<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu al-Abbas al-Saffah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/750">750</a>–754</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as al-Saffah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu al-Abbas al-Saffah was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, reigning from 750 to 754. He was proclaimed caliph during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a>, and his forces defeated the last Umayyad caliph. His short reign saw the consolidation of Abbasid power and the elimination of many members of the Umayyad family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-al-abbas-al-saffah.jpg" alt="Abu al-Abbas al-Saffah" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abu Ali Bal'ami · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balami_-_Tarikhnama_-_Abu%27l-%27Abbas_al-Saffah_is_proclaimed_the_first_%27Abbasid_Caliph_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
